========================================================================
V3 -- gate-level datapath vs the software integer model (.OP)
========================================================================

V3a  full adder, exhaustive (8 cases)
  [PASS] sum and carry exact
        converged 8/8 (100%), exact 8/8

V3b  2-bit ripple adder, exhaustive (16 cases)
  [PASS] hardware sum == integer sum (mod 2^n)
        converged 16/16 (100%), exact 16/16

V3c  2x2 array multiplier, exhaustive (16 cases)
  [PASS] hardware product == integer product
        converged 14/16 (88%), exact 14/14

V3d  measured .OP convergence ceiling
        2-bit adder    88 MOS  converges
        3-bit adder   132 MOS  converges
        4-bit adder   176 MOS  does NOT converge
        5-bit adder   220 MOS  does NOT converge
  ceiling ~132 transistors per DC solve. A full INT8 multiplier is
  ~3800 transistors and is NOT claimed to have been simulated; what is
  verified is that every primitive it is built from is exact.

========================================================================
V3 PASSED -- every datapath primitive is exact on every possible input.
